From a2fa91bffc3debd52dd64d343ecf627c4340582c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:58:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test(host-contracts): Level 0 retirement tests on the
 0.14 line, with U6

Main's Level 0 tests (8e2cd34b) ported to ACL v0.5.0/v0.5.1 by
impl/harness/phase4/port_l0_tests_v014.py: the baseline fixture is
v0.5.0, ACL v0.5.x has no isDelegatedForUserDecryption (its answer is
rebuilt as main computes it), revocation is pause-gated on this line,
and the gas test compares v0.5.0 with v0.5.1.

The upgrade matrix is rewritten for this line, with U6: v0.4.0, v0.4.1
and v0.5.0 upgrade to v0.5.1 with state and enforcement preserved; our
v0.13 E1 release (v0.4.2) collides with v0.5.1 on reinitializer 7 and
its upgrade call reverts, and without the call E1 is dropped. New
fixtures: ACL v0.4.2 with its own events, and v0.5.1 drift and
attribution variants. The Hardhat upgrade test expects v0.5.1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
